      "title": "All passengers and crew accounted for after New Orleans boat crash in ‘miracle on the Mississippi’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/13/mississippi-river-crash-new-orleans",
      "description": "<p>No passengers or crew killed or critically hurt after tanker collides with river cruise ship on Mississippi, officials say</p><p>In what the city’s mayor declared a “miracle on the Mississippi”, all passengers were accounted for – with none killed or critically hurt – after a tanker collided with a river cruise ship docked on the Mississippi River in <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/new-orleans\">New Orleans</a> on Friday afternoon.</p><p>Thirty-two people were taken to local hospitals after the Atlantic Asphalt tanker struck American Cruise Lines’s American Heritage at about 12.30pm – but none of their injuries were considered critical, New Orleans’s mayor, Helena Moreno, said at a news conference.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/13/mississippi-river-crash-new-orleans\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
